vidence/record-0abd9e0edd.md\r\n# record-0abd9e0edd: review of record-486aab454e\r\nRecorded 2026-07-18. Subject: Sunday Room; alias: triage facets. Action record-f724a71637; revision record-562146c9ea.11.1; cohort US enterprise administrators; observation 2026-07-07 through 2026-07-14.\r\nCorrection: A region migration had assigned older activity to the account's new region. The estimate for support contacts changes from +5.0% to +3.9%. Its definition remains new contacts about the named surface, excluding follow-up replies. The correction only covers this record's enrollment and observation window.\r\nReview of the recordings: the wording preference remains qualitative evidence. Changing the aggregate interpretation does not undo an actual deployment, rollback, customer contact, or disabled pilot.\r\nNext observation: the next settled-outcome ledger for this enrollment. The neighboring regional rollout uses a different source ID and is not superseded by this correction.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n/workspace/product/history/evidence/record-9f06ab8c13.md\r\n# record-9f06ab8c13: review of record-534278fd14\r\nRecorded 2026-03-22. Subject: triage facets; alias: weekly note. Action record-4024585246; revision record-8ff9b086a1.16.2; cohort Brazilian free workspaces; observation 2026-03-06 through 2026-03-14.\r\nCorrection: The job reconciler found a completed operation whose first acknowledgement had timed out. The estimate for first-week activation changes from -3.0% to -3.6%. Its definition remains new accounts completing the stated onboarding task within seven days. The correction only covers this record's enrollment and observation window.\r\nReview of the recordings: the count query still needs a separate performance check. Changing the aggregate interpretation does not undo an actual deployment, rollback, customer contact, or disabled pilot.\r\nNext observation: a paired check on the oldest supported client. The neighboring regional rollout uses a different source ID and is not superseded by this correction.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n/workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md\r\n# Desktop status filter rollout\r\nAction record-40440b02ae, record-3984af46e2, deployed August 30 to all desktop accounts, receipt record-764afbf446. Count queries are asynchronous. Desktop small-workspace smoke checks pass. Mobile clients remain on the old list and have no filter control; the mobile component is a draft. This release does not claim mobile availability.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n/workspace/product/history/actions/record-ecc0d14c71.md\r\n# record-ecc0d14c71: Focus Shelf\r\nAliases: triage facets; status filters. Internal name record-e9d336d487. Deployed May 14 to enterprise desktop accounts only, receipt record-226210156c. Android and iOS were not included. Initial record-8a2203deaa reported 2% weekly use. Rolled back June 2, receipt record-929bef0cdc, after slow count queries in workspaces over 50,000 tasks.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n/workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md\r\n# Weekly feedback export\r\nRetrieved 2026-09-07. Ticket record-e36f0fe1aa, submitted 2026-09-05: Solo owner on Android 15, workspace with 34 tasks: 'On desktop I can narrow to waiting, but on my phone I have to scroll through everything.'\r\nTicket record-5f1a34c149, submitted unknown: contributor in a 280-person EU team, client web 6.8: 'The quiet digest still pings me every evening. I only need the weekly note.' The connector supplies age_days=20; its definition is days since digest release, not ticket age.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n/workspace/product/history/retired/notification-reset/brief.md\r\n# notification-reset\r\nBounded responsibility terminated July 31 after preference migration. Its action and preference audit records are retained for continuing product work.\r\n\r\n-----------------------------